.TH AIWR 1
.SH NAME
aiwr \- inspect and clean AI watermark and provenance metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aiwr
.I command
.RI [ options ] " path ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aiwr
is a Go command-line tool for inspecting and cleaning deterministic Unicode
marks, file metadata, provenance containers, and optional watermark backends.
It defaults to writing a new output and never overwrites an input unless
.B --in-place
is explicitly selected.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B clean
Clean a file, directory, or batch of files.
.TP
.B inspect
Inspect a file or directory without modifying it.
.TP
.B detect
Emit detection-oriented output.
.TP
.B audit
Audit a directory and optionally emit JSON or SARIF.
.TP
.B clean-text
Clean text from a path or stdin.
.TP
.B serve
Run the local HTTP API.
.SH DIRECTORY OUTPUT
A directory is written to a sibling directory named
.I DIRECTORY.cleaned
with relative names, modes, and symbolic links preserved. Unchanged files may
use reflink when supported and selected with
.B --reflink auto
or
.B --reflink always.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means success without actionable residuals, 1 means a finding or residual,
2 means invalid arguments or refusal, and 3 means partial batch failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aiwr (1)
.SH AUTHOR
aiwr contributors
